WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.063
In Active Directory, where an object
sits decides how it's governed.

2
00:00:04.063 --> 00:00:06.930
Move a user to another
organizational unit (OU),

3
00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:12.212
and their administrators and policies
change without anyone touching the account.

4
00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:16.790
Entra ID has no tree; it governs
by what an object carries:

5
00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.676
attributes, memberships and roles.

6
00:00:19.676 --> 00:00:23.525
So every placement-based rule
has to be rewritten explicitly.

7
00:00:23.525 --> 00:00:28.274
Administrative units (AUs) help, but
they can't nest, and for synced users

8
00:00:28.274 --> 00:00:33.350
the attributes are still written
on-premises, so every change waits on sync.

9
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:37.873
That makes one decision come early:
which attributes are authoritative,

10
00:00:37.873 --> 00:00:40.662
what they mean, and where
each one is mastered.

11
00:00:40.662 --> 00:00:45.001
HR decides the meaning, and identity
engineering decides the flow.

12
00:00:45.001 --> 00:00:49.150
But first, which of this is the
job of Identity and Directory.
